## Hoenn: widen the trainer flag space (src/hoenn_trainer_flags.c)
##   Vanilla maps a trainer to flag 0x500 + id, and 0x800 is SYS_FLAGS,
##   so the ceiling is trainer 767. Vanilla already uses up to 742, which
##   leaves 25 slots; the 8 Hoenn gyms alone need 65.
##   New mapping: id < 768 -> 0x500 + id (unchanged, Kanto is untouched)
##                id >= 768 -> 0x1400 + (id - 768)   (expanded flags)
##   The whole game builds a trainer flag in only these 4 ROM functions
##   plus 5 spots in CFRU's overworld.c (patches/0038). Checked against
##   pokefirered by grepping TRAINER_FLAGS_START, and the BL counts below
##   were measured in the ROM and match the decomp.
##   Each of these is >= 20 bytes and nothing branches into the middle
##   (CLAUDE.md 6.22; verify_trainer_flags.py checks it every time).
HoennGetTrainerAFlag 0807F7D8 0 1
HoennHasTrainerBeenFought 0807FB44 1 1
HoennSetTrainerFlag 0807FB5C 1 0
HoennClearTrainerFlag 0807FB70 1 0

## Hoenn: Route 118 plays two different songs (src/hoenn_music.c)
##   The Emerald map header stores MUS_ROUTE118 (0x7FFF), which is not a
##   song but a marker: west of x=24 plays MUS_ROUTE110, east plays
##   MUS_ROUTE119 (pokeemerald/src/overworld.c GetCurrLocationDefaultMusic).
##   Vanilla FireRed has no such branch, so the value fell through to the
##   "song not ported" default and a Kanto track played instead.
##   GetLocationMusic is 32 bytes and nothing branches into it past its
##   entry (CLAUDE.md 6.22; tools/bgm/verify_hoenn_bgm.py checks it).
##   Only two callers, and every other map returns the header value
##   unchanged, so Kanto is untouched.
HoennGetLocationMusic 0805562C 1 1

## Hoenn: Ever Grande has two fly destinations (src/hoenn_townmap.c)
##   The mapsec spans two town map cells: the upper one is the Pokemon
##   League, the lower one is the city. Emerald picks by posWithinMapSec
##   (region_map.c:2007); vanilla FireRed stores one destination per
##   mapsec, so the whole function is replaced and the heal index is
##   swapped when the cursor sits on the upper cell.
##   SetFlyWarpDestination is 84 bytes and nothing branches into the 20
##   bytes we overwrite (CLAUDE.md 6.22; verify_townmap.py checks it).
HoennSetFlyWarpDestination 080C6460 1 0

